		<Item class="ModuleScript" referent="RBX16FD667544634566BA20170A14FE1EF3">
			<Properties>
				<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
				<ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--[[
	MASCOTS  —  the cartoon characters (ModuleScript in ReplicatedStorage): CPU racers
	drive as them, players can pick one in the garage menu to drive as instead of
	their own avatar, and they cheer in the grandstands. RaceServer builds them with
	Mascots.build(); GarageClient uses it for the menu's 3D previews.

	Every character gets the same simple body: a round body, two arms, a head and
	two eyes. What makes each one different is listed in its entry:
	  name       what the garage menu calls it (default: its id, like "Fox")
	  kart       colour of its kart (and racing suit)
	  fur        colour of its head (and hands)
	  body       colour of its body, if it isn't wearing a racing suit (a penguin is black)
	  hands      colour of its hands (default: fur)
	  head       size of its head (default 2.2 wide, 2 tall, 2 deep)
	  headShape  "Block" for a boxy head (the robot)
	  eyes       false = no standard eyes (it lists its own, like the frog's)
	  eyeY / eyeSpread / eyeZ / eyeScale   move and size the standard eyes
	  extras     ears, noses, tails...: { s = shape, size, at = position, color, rot, pair, mat, alpha }
	             s: "Egg" (a ball you can stretch), "Ball", "Block", "Cylinder" or "Wedge"
	             at: studs from the middle of the head; -Z is the way it faces
	             rot: degrees to turn it (x, y, z)
	             pair = true adds a mirror copy on the other side (ears, eyes, whiskers)
	             color: a Color3, or "Fur"
	BOTS.MASCOTS in RaceServer says which racer is which character, and THEMES
	say which characters cheer in each track's grandstand.
]]

